WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.834
-Our next guest is a talented
actress who stars in

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:06.434
and executive-produces the
television series "The Great,"

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:07.834
which is streaming now on Hulu.

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:09.734
Please welcome Elle Fanning,
everybody.

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:10.767
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:13.334
Oh! Hi, pal. Oh!

00:00:13.334 --> 00:00:15.100
I miss you.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:18.200
Elle, you have such a --
You have a glow around you.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.033
It's like you're a --
like a beautiful --

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:23.734
-No, I didn't realize
this top is, like,

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:25.734
shimmering in the L.A. sun.

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:29.167
-Wow! You look like a fairy --
a magical fairy.

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:31.200
[ CHOIR VOCALIZING ]
♪ Ahhh ♪

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.100
Yeah, I love this.
Welcome to our show.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.033
Welcome back. How are you?
How is the family?

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:39.200
Everyone good?
-Everyone's really good.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.300
I wish I was there,
like, sitting on the couch.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.567
It made me jealous
watching Kenan.

00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:46.067
I haven't been to New York
in so long.

00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:48.100
-Well, you'll get here.
-But I'm with family.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.567
-Yep, very good.
Very soon, we'll do it.

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:53.367
Did you celebrate New Year's
with the fam?

00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:54.634
What did you do?

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:57.701
-You know, we had some plans
that we actually --

00:00:57.701 --> 00:01:00.701
we had to cancel, but we
normally go to my sister's.

00:01:00.701 --> 00:01:05.033
And she has a party of some kind
with a bunch of her friends,

00:01:05.033 --> 00:01:06.400
and I always go over there.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.834
And this year,
she was super-excited,

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:10.434
'cause she came up
with this idea

00:01:10.434 --> 00:01:14.200
that she was going to do
a fast-food potluck.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:17.067
-Wait. What is this about?
I like the idea, though.

00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:19.801
-Yeah, everyone was going
to bring a different fast food.

00:01:19.801 --> 00:01:22.667
We had, like, Taco Bell,
McDonald's, Domino's,

00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:26.567
Krispy Kreme, like,
and I was in charge of Popeyes.

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:28.634
-Oh, my gosh!
-I know.

00:01:28.634 --> 00:01:30.400
It's so sad
that it didn't happen.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.601
-Oh! I want to go to this party.
-Yeah.

00:01:33.601 --> 00:01:35.234
-Next time you come to New York,
let's do it.

00:01:35.234 --> 00:01:36.868
Let's just start one up.
Potluck fast food --

00:01:36.868 --> 00:01:39.300
-Yeah, it's a cute idea.
We love fast food, so...

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:40.501
-I've got to do
the McDonald's, man.

00:01:40.501 --> 00:01:43.100
I've got to do --
-Yeah, you bring the McDonald's.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:44.467
-I'll do the Mickey D'S,
yeah, yeah.

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:45.601
Exactly, yeah.
-Cool.

00:01:45.601 --> 00:01:47.501
You know,
I want to ask you this question.

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:50.100
This is a -- You know me.
I get down to it.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.901
I want -- I'm hard-hitting,
ask the real questions.

00:01:52.901 --> 00:01:56.033
And I want to know about this.

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:57.200
There's a rumor online --

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:00.801
look at this right here --
that on TikTok,

00:02:00.801 --> 00:02:08.133
user6754189318472 --

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:10.801
fans think that that is you.

00:02:10.801 --> 00:02:12.934
Can you confirm or deny?

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.367
-I confirm that is me.
-Wow!

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:20.067
It is you.

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:21.901
It's such a catchy --

00:02:21.901 --> 00:02:24.167
Clearly, you're doing this
for the followers,

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:25.200
because it's such a catchy --

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.567
-I know.
It's so easy to memorize.

00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:28.467
-Easy to remember,
yeah, of course.

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:30.934
"Oh, I'm user 67584--"
Yeah, exactly.

00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:33.734
Why is that your name,
by the way?

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:36.133
-God, you know, I think in the
first lockdown, like --

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:37.534
I say "first lockdown."

00:02:37.534 --> 00:02:41.267
But, like, right when everything
started, TikTok so exploded.

00:02:41.267 --> 00:02:44.167
And I was with my friend.
He's like, "You should make one.

00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:46.033
Like, let's see what happens.
Just do it.

00:02:46.033 --> 00:02:48.734
Don't put a profile picture.

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:51.467
Just don't change the name.
And let's see."

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:55.000
And I posted,
and it kind of, like --

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.667
It got a lot of followers.

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:59.667
And, like, TikTok then DM'd me
on my Instagram

00:02:59.667 --> 00:03:03.267
and was like, you know, "You've
surpassed this certain number."

00:03:03.267 --> 00:03:04.968
Like, I was just doing it
as a joke,

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:07.534
but I don't know.

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:10.334
I post when I want.
But it's silly.

00:03:10.334 --> 00:03:12.968
It's like little secret.
Not so secret, I guess, now.

00:03:12.968 --> 00:03:14.667
-No, now it's out, yeah.
-Thanks.

00:03:14.667 --> 00:03:16.167
-I want to talk --
Let's talk about "The Great."

00:03:16.167 --> 00:03:18.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:21.033
It's fantastic.

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:23.501
You are such a good actor.

00:03:23.501 --> 00:03:25.033
Congrats on -- You're getting
all sorts of

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:27.033
awards and nominations.

00:03:27.033 --> 00:03:28.534
Congratulations.

00:03:28.534 --> 00:03:32.267
Season 2
streaming right now on Hulu.

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:34.834
Do you want to set up what's
going on in this season?

00:03:34.834 --> 00:03:37.634
-Yes. This season,
Catherine has --

00:03:37.634 --> 00:03:41.501
The coup has worked, and she's
successfully overthrown

00:03:41.501 --> 00:03:42.968
her husband, Peter,

00:03:42.968 --> 00:03:46.434
which is played by the amazing,
hilarious Nicholas Hoult.

00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:47.701
-He is great.

00:03:47.701 --> 00:03:50.100
-And now, basically,
I mean, the whole of Russia,

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.834
the country,
is on Catherine's shoulders,

00:03:51.834 --> 00:03:54.400
and she has to learn how to be
a mother to a country

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.501
and a mother
to her unborn child.

00:03:57.501 --> 00:03:59.200
She's pregnant
throughout the season.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:02.167
-Yeah. You know,
you posted this online,

00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:04.334
and I was like,
"What is going on?

00:04:04.334 --> 00:04:05.634
And was this in the script?"

00:04:05.634 --> 00:04:07.801
But can you describe
what's happening here?

00:04:07.801 --> 00:04:09.701
You're pregnant.
-Yeah.

00:04:09.701 --> 00:04:14.400
Yes, that is me doing
a backbend on set

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.767
with my bump,
which was incorporated

00:04:17.767 --> 00:04:19.767
into the scene,
actually, somehow.

00:04:19.767 --> 00:04:21.033
-How?

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:24.467
-They wanted to show kind of
Catherine in, like,

00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:28.000
a fun way and they wanted her to
do a party trick of some kind.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.734
And I was trying to come up with
what I could do.

00:04:30.734 --> 00:04:32.734
So I asked Tony,
our showrunner --

00:04:32.734 --> 00:04:34.734
I was like,
"I can do a backbend."

00:04:34.734 --> 00:04:38.000
So they -- But he was like,
"Can you really?"

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.734
So, it preceded with me, like,
having to go, like,

00:04:40.734 --> 00:04:44.501
do a show-and-tell to, like, the
props, the set, the costumers,

00:04:44.501 --> 00:04:47.033
like, to see if I really could
and if it actually worked.

00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:51.400
And, so, I was serving macaroons
on my pregnant tummy.

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:52.501
Fake pregnant tummy.

00:04:52.501 --> 00:04:54.400
-That's crazy
how those things happen.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:57.100
I know -- I heard,
at the end of every season,

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:02.234
you paint a portrait of you
as Catherine?

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:03.567
-I do, I do.

00:05:03.567 --> 00:05:05.767
You know,
each film I've ever done,

00:05:05.767 --> 00:05:07.200
every director
I have worked with,

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:11.934
I have given them a little,
like, drawing of my character.

00:05:11.934 --> 00:05:15.234
So, I did this for
the director and Tony

00:05:15.234 --> 00:05:17.701
on the pilot, actually.

00:05:17.701 --> 00:05:20.000
It's, like, silly.
-You're very talented.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.534
I love these.

00:05:21.534 --> 00:05:25.300
-They're, like,
little cartoony, but -- Yeah.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.834
-Do people, like, ask you to do
their portraits now?

00:05:27.834 --> 00:05:32.033
Like, people are like, "Hey,
could you do one of me" or --

00:05:32.033 --> 00:05:35.901
-Well, I guess I would be up
for the challenge,

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:39.200
but they all kind of
end up looking like me,

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:42.400
because I only draw myself.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.968
-So if you did me, it'd be your
face in a suit behind a desk.

00:05:45.968 --> 00:05:47.167
-Yes, exactly.

00:05:47.167 --> 00:05:51.767
Little cropped, you know,
brunet hair, but my face.

00:05:51.767 --> 00:05:53.934
So if you want that.
-Yeah, I do.

00:05:53.934 --> 00:05:55.501
Who wouldn't want your face?
Are you kidding me?

00:05:55.501 --> 00:05:57.734
Come on.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:57.734 --> 00:06:00.067
Here's Elle Fanning in Season 2
of "The Great."

00:06:00.067 --> 00:06:01.667
Take a look at this.

00:06:01.667 --> 00:06:05.567
-How blessed we are by our Lord.

00:06:05.567 --> 00:06:08.534
I bless Catherine the Great,

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:09.701
for she is our
new and rightful sovereign.

00:06:09.701 --> 00:06:11.367
-You're calling yourself
"The Great"?

00:06:11.367 --> 00:06:12.467
-Of course.

00:06:12.467 --> 00:06:13.901
-Bow before her
in worship and praise.

00:06:13.901 --> 00:06:16.267
-It seems arrogant.

00:06:16.267 --> 00:06:18.067
-It is if you are not great.

00:06:18.067 --> 00:06:20.501
If you are, it is just calling
things what they are.

00:06:20.501 --> 00:06:22.000
-Right.
-Shh!

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.000
-I have a speech.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.834
-Just put on
the crown on me when

00:06:24.834 --> 00:06:26.434
the long-winded blessing stops

00:06:26.434 --> 00:06:28.367
or I will have you
dragged out right now.

00:06:28.367 --> 00:06:29.467
-You wouldn't.

00:06:29.467 --> 00:06:31.734
-It would be embarrassing
for us both

00:06:31.734 --> 00:06:33.767
and make it clear I took it.

00:06:33.767 --> 00:06:36.434
So maybe it is a good idea.

00:06:36.434 --> 00:06:37.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:37.434 --> 00:06:39.133
-Elle Fanning, everyone!

00:06:39.133 --> 00:06:42.300
Season 2 of "The Great"
is streaming now on Hulu.

